# Composability

Frontend reviewers will look for composition, not copy-paste. One primitive, many call sites. File placement is in `atomic-design.mdc`.

- Do not duplicate JSX, className stacks, or parse/fetch logic. Extract.
- Pages assemble organisms and molecules. They do not inline atoms.
- Compose with `children` and slots. Do not grow a prop bag of booleans (`isLarge`, `showIcon`, `variant2`).
- A second copy is a bug. If you are about to paste, extract first — into the lowest atomic layer that fits.
- Clear atoms (hash, amount, input, empty/error) exist from the first use.

```tsx
// ❌ same type soup in three files
<p className="border border-border text-secondary">{label}</p>

// ✅ molecule + organism
<Narrative>
  <Narrative.Lead>{lead}</Narrative.Lead>
  <Narrative.Fact label="from">{from}</Narrative.Fact>
</Narrative>
```

Keep each component one job. No kitchen-sink `FlexibleCard`.
